WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:02.780
Here's a fact that surprises people.

2
00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:08.251
The idea that the universe is expanding was first published by a Catholic priest.

3
00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.727
His name was Georges Lemaître.

4
00:00:10.727 --> 00:00:14.306
He was ordained in nineteen twenty-three, in Belgium,

5
00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:16.197
and he was also a physicist.

6
00:00:16.197 --> 00:00:23.627
In nineteen twenty-seven he published a paper showing that Einstein's equations allowed a universe that grows,

7
00:00:23.627 --> 00:00:30.178
and that distant galaxies should be moving away from us at speeds proportional to their distance.

8
00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:33.960
Edwin Hubble's famous observations came two years later.

9
00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.963
A few years after that,

10
00:00:35.963 --> 00:00:40.826
Lemaître proposed that the universe began from a single "primeval atom".

11
00:00:40.826 --> 00:00:43.595
That's the idea we now call the Big Bang.

12
00:00:44.045 --> 00:00:51.745
In twenty eighteen the International Astronomical Union recommended renaming Hubble's law the Hubble-Lemaître law.

13
00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:55.707
He saw no war between his collar and his chalkboard.

14
00:00:55.707 --> 00:00:59.759
The Catechism puts it simply: truth cannot contradict truth.

15
00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:04.959
The same God made the mind that does the maths and the universe it describes.
